.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH tapectl-volume-deposit-add 1  "tapectl-volume-deposit-add " 
.SH NAME
tapectl\-volume\-deposit\-add \- Record that a sealed volume\*(Aqs bytes now also exist at a warehouse
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtapectl volume deposit add\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] <\fB\-\-to\fR> [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-receipt\fR] [\fB\-\-storage\-class\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-notes\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fILABEL\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Record that a sealed volume\*(Aqs bytes now also exist at a warehouse
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output in JSON format
.TP
\fB\-\-to\fR \fI<TO>\fR
Warehouse location name (must be a location of kind `warehouse`)
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would be done without making changes
.TP
\fB\-\-receipt\fR \fI<RECEIPT>\fR
The provider\*(Aqs receipt / object\-version identifier, if it gave one. There is deliberately no checksum field: tapectl did not perform the copy, so a typed\-in checksum would be a claim about a claim (issue #73)
.TP
\fB\-\-storage\-class\fR \fI<STORAGE_CLASS>\fR
Storage class the bytes were placed in (e.g. DEEP_ARCHIVE)
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable verbose output
.TP
\fB\-\-notes\fR \fI<NOTES>\fR
Free\-text note
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip confirmation prompts
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
Path to config file
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fILABEL\fR>
Volume label whose bytes were deposited
